  "published": false,
  "change": "Enhanced liquids use the authored tile palettes without painted line detail. Clear water retains its animated ripples; swamps use opaque, mottled duckweed with restrained reflection; lava uses animated hot patches and darker crust.",
  "implementation": {
    "source": "game/src/ei/terrain.gd",
    "metadata": "Bit 16 in the existing float tile table selects an authored tile average; all original 16-bit tile/atlas/rotation codes and absent-tile sentinels remain intact.",
    "sampling": "The mip level is selected from actual atlas dimensions so original 512px and HD 2048px atlases each contribute one texel per authored tile, sampled at its centre.",
    "material_detail": "Reuse the existing foam noise for world-space swamp coverage and molten patches. Swamp opacity is 0.93\u20130.995 away from the soft shoreline; the reflection contribution is capped at 0.015 and native additive wave highlights are excluded.",
    "resources": "No additional texture, sampler, mesh or draw pass; swamp adds two noise reads, lava one. No FPS improvement claim.",
    "unchanged": [
      "Original-look water shader",
      "land shader",
      "clear-water foam, transparency, scene reflection and wave logic",
      "caustics option",
      "collision/navigation and liquid surface geometry"
    ],
    "new_player_visible_strings": 0
  },
  "diagnosis": {
    "painted_lines": "Long repeating lines were present in the authored liquid atlases, especially apparent with HD replacement atlases.",
    "preview_blue_wash": "The earlier zone1/zone7 surface captures were near map edges. EITerrain.load_map reset the border-fog setting after the fixture initially disabled it; that fog caused the large cyan wash. The corrected comparison disables border fog after each load, equally for before and after. Production border fog is unchanged.",
    "earlier_preservation_check": "The initial 16 original/HD captures proved swamp/lava unchanged by the clear-water-only edit. That was a preservation check, not visual acceptance; it is superseded by the deliberate material changes and the final captures below."
  },
